Design choices made and trade-offs
Chose AWS EC2 for managed VMs, autoscaling, revisions, and AMI artifacts.
Trade-off: more control and management, less flexibility than containers with deployments.

Problems I ran into, and how to troubleshoot them?
Permissions that allowed GitHub to access the SSM Parameter Store to update the AMI ID with the new deployment image.

What did I learn from the project?
How to build AWS infra with Terraform 
How to use and apply IAM access with Terraform.
How to design safer deployment workflows.
Canary-style deployment with target groups updating the AMI of registered targets after a deployment.
How to troubleshoot across Terraform, Azure, containers, and the application.

What would I change if this were supporting real production traffic?
Add Web Application Firewall (WAF).
Deploy across multiple regions.
Increase staging and production isolation.
Improve monitoring, alerting, and security scanning.
Blue/green deployments.
